Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

_3D.addObject [SimTalk]
Creates an animatable object for the object designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.addObject(Name:string[, LengthOriented:boolean]) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Name of data type string designates the name of the animatable object.
Specify a name, which corresponds to the name of an animatable object in the origin of the object,
in which the new animatable object is going to be created to create an object that inherits from the
animatable object in the origin of the respective object. This way you can restore a deleted animatable
object, which inherits from another object, in a way that it inherits again from the original object.
• The optional parameter LengthOriented of data type boolean sets if the animatable object is to be
length-oriented (true) or not (false).
If you specify this parameter and the object would be created with an origin, the newly created object
will only have an origin if this origin is length-oriented as well if you set it to true.
This is not the case if you specify false.
Specify this parameter to make the new object length-oriented if it has an origin and if this origin is
length-oriented as well.
Return Value
The return value has the data type any.
It is the newly created object.
Examples
// adds an animatable object to the Station
var MyAnimatableObject := Station._3D.addObject("MyAnimatableObject")
// deletes the animatable object from the Station
_3D.addObject [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-669
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

MyAnimatableObject.delete
Station._3D.getObject("MyAnimatableObject").delete
// adds an animatable object to the Conveyor
// and makes it length-oriented
var MyAnimatableObject := Conveyor._3D.addObject("MyAnimatableObject", true)
