_3D.getMUAnimationRotation [SimTalk]
Returns the rotation with which a MU would be animated under certain marginal conditions.
Remarks
You can call _3D.getMUAnimationRotation for length-oriented objects and for point-oriented objects.
getMUAnimationRotation for Length-oriented Objects
Returns the anticipated rotation of a MU on the length-oriented object designated by <Path>.
If you call the method for a simulation object, the method evaluates the attribute _3D.AnimationObject
and, if need be, makes the rotation of the animated object part of the computation.
If you call the method for the animatable object itself, the method only considers this object. Plant
Simulation assumes that the animation will take place on this animatable object and returns the rotation
within the coordinate system of the animatable object.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.getMUAnimationRotation(RelPos/AbsPos:real/length[, Lane/
Direction:integer:=1]) -> real[4]
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter RelPos/AbsPos is a value of data type real or length.
If the value has the data type real, it designates the rotation at the relative position on the object. The
relative position can be a value between 0 and 1. 0 designates the start of the animation and 1 the end
of the animation, i.e., the value 100 %.
If the value has the data type length, it designates the rotation at the absolute position on the object.
• The optional parameter Lane/Direction of data type integer designates the lane or the direction on the
object respectively.
For a TwoLaneTrack the value 1 designates lane A and the value 2 designates lane B.
For a Converter the value 1 designates the default direction and the value 2 cross-wise conveying.
For all other objects 1 is the only valid value. If you do not specify the value, Plant Simulation
automatically uses the value 1.
_3D.getMUAnimationRotation [SimTalk]
12-680 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is 1.
Return Value
The return value is an array of data type real with four values.
Example
var p := Converter._3D.getMUAnimationRotation(0.5, 2)
var p := Conveyor._3D.getMUAnimationRotation(1m)
getMUAnimationRotation for Point-oriented Objects
Returns the anticipated rotation of a MU on the point-oriented object designated by <Path>.
If you call the method for a simulation object, the method evaluates the attribute _3D.AnimationObject
and, if need be, makes the rotation of the animated object part of the computation.
If you call the method for the animatable object itself, the method only considers this object. Plant
Simulation assumes that the animation will take place on this animatable object and returns the rotation
within the coordinate system of the animatable object.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.getMUAnimationRotation([X:integer:=1, Y:integer:=1]) -> real[4]
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The optional parameter X of data type integer designates the processing place in the X-direction.
You have to enter the parameter for objects with a matrix loading space.
For other objects the parameter is optional. If you do not specify the value, Plant Simulation
automatically uses the value 1.
For objects, which only have a single processing place, 1 is the only valid value.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is 1.
_3D.getMUAnimationRotation [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-681
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• The optional parameter Y of data type integer designates the processing place in the Y-direction.
You have to enter the parameter for objects with a matrix loading space.
For other objects the parameter is optional. If you do not specify the value, Plant Simulation
automatically uses the value 1.
For objects, which only have a single processing place, 1 is the only valid value.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is 1.
Return Value
The return value is an array of data type real with four values.
Examples
var p := Station._3D.getMUAnimationRotation()
var p := PlaceBuffer._3D.getMUAnimationRotation(4)
var p := ParallelStation._3D.getMUAnimationRotation(3,4)
