_3D.Mirror [SimTalk]
Sets mirroring of the object designated by <Path> on one or three planes.
Remarks
Mirroring does not apply to existing length-oriented objects, moving objects (MUs), and to Connectors.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.Mirror:boolean/boolean[3]
Assignment Value
You can specify:
• A single value of data type boolean to only mirror the object on the YZ-Plane.
• A value of data type array containing three values of data type boolean to set mirroring around the
designated planes. The values of data type boolean designate the YZ-Plane, the XZ-Plane, and the
XY-Plane in this order.
Examples
MyFrame._3D.Mirror := true
MyFrame._3D.Mirror := [true,false,true]
See also
Settings for Mirroring
_3D.Mirror [SimTalk]
12-706 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

