_3D.Rotation [SimTalk]
Sets the current rotation of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
For an MU instance, _3D.Rotation will not affect the simulation-relevant rotation of the MU. To change the
simulation-relevant rotation, use ConveyingDirection instead.
For an AGV, you can also use the parameter named Angle of the method setWorldPosition to affect the
simulation-relevant rotation.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.Rotation:real/real[4]
Assignment Value
You can specify:
• A number which defines the rotation around the negative z-axis at the position at which you inserted
the object.
• An array of data type real with four items, which defines the rotation around the specified axis (values 2
to 4) at the position at which you inserted the object.
If you get the attribute, 3D returns an array with four items.
Examples
var a : any := MyStation._3D.Rotation
// returns an array of 4 values
MyStation._3D.Rotation := 30
// rotates the object by 30 degrees
MyStation._3D.Rotation := [45, 0, 1, 0]
// rotates the object by 45 degrees around the Y axis
_3D.Rotation [SimTalk]
12-708 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

