F3DconcatenateRotations [SimTalk]
Concatenates two rotations into one and returns the computed value.
Type
Method
Syntax
F3DconcatenateRotations(Rotation1:real[4], Rotation2:real[4]) → real[4]
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Rotation1 is an array of data type real with four values, which sets the first rotation
of the graphic. The elements of the array denote the rotation angle, and the x-component, the
y-component, and the z-component of the rotation axis.
• The parameter Rotation2 is an array of data type real with four values, which sets the second rotation
of the graphic. The elements of the array denote the rotation angle, and the x-component, the
y-component, and the z-component of the rotation axis.
Return Value
The return value is an array with four values of data type real.
It corresponds to the sequence of the input rotations which are executed one after the other in the
sequence in which they were passed to the method.
Examples
Station._3D.Rotation := F3DconcatenateRotations(Station._3D.Rotation, [45, 
0, 1, 0])
Station._3D.Rotation := F3DconcatenateRotations([90, 0, 1, 0], [45, 0, 1, 
0])
See also
_3D.Rotation [SimTalk]
Rotation [SimTalk] - graphic
F3DconcatenateRotations [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-713
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

