_3D.BoundingBoxMax minus _3D.BoundingBoxMin results in the _3D.BoundingBoxSize.
_3D.BoundingBoxMax has to be equal to or greater than _3D.BoundingBoxMin.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.BoundingBoxMin → length[3]
Return Value
The return value is an array of data type length with three values.
The values designate the X-Position, the Y-Position, and the Z-Position of the lower left vertex of the
bounding box.
Example
var a : length[3] := MyStation._3D.BoundingBoxMin
_3D.BoundingBoxMin [SimTalk]
12-728 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

_3D.BoundingBoxSize [SimTalk]
Returns the size of the bounding box of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The bounding box excludes all invisible graphics.
The bounding box of an object encloses its graphics and its animatable objects. In addition, the bounding
box of a Frame encloses its static simulation objects. A MU instance does not belong to the bounding box
of the object that is currently transporting it. The bounding box of a pallet does, for example, not include
the parts loaded onto the pallet.
The individual values of the bounding box relate to each other as follows:
_3D.BoundingBoxMin plus _3D.BoundingBoxMax divided by 2 results in the _3D.BoundingBoxCenter.
_3D.BoundingBoxMax minus _3D.BoundingBoxMin results in the _3D.BoundingBoxSize.
_3D.BoundingBoxMax has to be equal to or greater than _3D.BoundingBoxMin.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.BoundingBoxSize → array
Return Value
The return value has the data type array.
The return values designate the length (X-dimension), the width (Y-dimension), and the height (Z-
dimension) of the bounding box.
Example
var a : real[3] := MyStation._3D.BoundingBoxSize
_3D.BoundingBoxSize [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-729
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens